        <p>DOUBLE-BIIIMNIED HATS. mar' Only in the finest weather would one ve— to wear the erownless, double-brimmed (ti(‘)w which are not unlike a sailor in shape. brim—the under one—is of tulle; the uPPc:fil'e tine Chantilly lace, ..both finely pleated. ,1 brims rise -high the hair. Sonle‘A:l,4.. resembling these m'e the Niniehe hats, °r- hi ugh they possess crow-us, or, rather. ")rind ing for the head, these are perfectly not C" platelike, whilst, the. m ,brim rises up soe in w - at the bacic.</p>
