        <p>Foresters Confer. the 80th High Court of the Ancient Order 121: Poresters, which has been held this week in he Albert Hall, Manchester, the Warrington rodges were represented by Bros. P. M.. Roden, • Chrirnes, and E. A. Jones.</p>
        <p>• Territorial Camp. A. The Warrington Territorials are proceeding their annual camp training of fifteen days to uenbigh this year. The men parade at Ilea&amp; tarters on Sunday, 17th August, and travel to 441e8 14- special train. To-morrow the annual - lurch Parade takes place at St. Paul's Church.</p>
        <p>Labour Meetings. .t.,:r4 Independent Labour party are at present .4,73'i11g on a campaign in Warrington, and a pales of meetings have been held at Bridge the chief speaker being Mr. U. Wall- a member of the**Executive-Council.ot the and prospective Socialist candidate for entry.</p>
        <p>Farmers Want Rain. ne drought was the chief subject of discus- -441 nngst the farmers assembled at Warring- is: Market on Wednesday. • They now want n• Tu • a• lsid rnips were reported to be suffering erably from want of moisture. On the Tr" hand, the sunshine has brought on the (pieul crops rapidly, and harvest, at present, "lises to be an early one.</p>
        <p>Great Angling Contest. 444:arrington , anglers to-day are competing somei thelust of the best fishers of England n uil veld , annual contest for the Bridgewater al n Si • is • ~AtWe ge Shield. The venue of the contest 1- oet istown, and urards of 200 " men of the bm (I,: are The expected to ine the canal bank. . L, "at has , however, affected the water, and , asket, may not prove very heavy.</p>
        <p>• . Boys' Brigade in Camp. vtne •tr oYs. Brigade attached to Golborne- (et Baptist Church will encamp on the farm wet. Faulkner, Stretton Hall, Stretton, for a stren beginning• to-day (Saturday). The thn'llgth of the company is about twenty, plus officers and the chaplain (Rev. ff. Ogden). " officer in charge will Captain T. Davies.</p>
