        <p>u ch, Poresters at Bowl;. It' ReoetllrdaY a party of Foresters. including ,-.ollio„Bprinkling of the fair sex., journeyed to Tle ~n _ their annual Picnic and bow li g. ‘Alif, wasinilclay was gloriously fine, and. evweerYre kh,Nrits f.f_allnY holiday mood. Mete tilllval Diavur the mean, and imme(siwiaetreel ye con- -4t 1- 'll,l4ed-, celaineneed.. The gan.ie * e gitt4BlP SIX o'clock, when tea was served. litt% retto were again renewed until. the final lyrNlier ',led. after which the District Chief, I,IR Ni -thornas Roden, distributed the follow- 1' Ni s. 'ellow.zes I--Lady's prize scent spray. 'I, ttm, .; .&gt; - Gentlemen :1, set of cutlery, S. Lytn- ett,tl;:illlirit cabinet, J. Ditchfiehl: 3, copt/er. (74`• Fatley; 4, W. el, James; 5, W. I_Tosworth: I IL C'°114(11IIR.; 7, F. Ryder: S. H. C. Forster; Innino *ll Halford; 11. W. A. t; -• : 12, li. 10, . lii,be rt. 4, Ilerry: 13. J. Gatley ; li, T. GatleY; •21:(.1\7, • filli,l"4‘.: sell.:' 10, T. Fellows; 17, W. Bil)1Y; Li li". . e: 19, J. R (Hear(' 1 t.,n. J. Davies; I 0a47"; 22.._ J. W. Ditchfield; 23, 'P. Marsh; 25, E. Davenport; 2, M. Jones. •</p>
