. Baker; 3, J. Hampson. Six plants in bloom: 1, D. S. Bir- tell ; 2' J. _Hampson. Collections of iregetables (eight kinds): .1. E. Taylor; 2, J. Miller. Dish of neas (eighteen pods); 1, J. Carmen; 2, E. Mills; 3, E. W. Whitehouse. Six vases of gar- den flowers: 1, J. Hampson ; 2, H. Taylor. Best decorated dinner table: 1, Mrs. F. Broady; 2, Mrs. Hargreaves: 3. Mrs. Mottram; c, Miss B. E.- Woodcock. Most effective display in hang- - jug basket: 1, F. A. Rathbone; 2, D. S. B. Birrell.</p>
        <p>OUTSIDE EXHIBITS. FOR MEMBERS ONLY. 1,-,-1.-17.Tf. besi--sfrw•lted den : 1. Edwin Taylor; 2, F. Kippax ; 3, E. Mille. The neatest and best-arranged garden (area not</p>
