      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-08-09_WidnesExaminer_art0225" n="art0225">
        <head>STIFF TUSSLE PREDICTED.</head>
        <p>STIFF TUSSLE PREDICTED.</p>
        <p>Final day in the works competition is reached. To-day will decide which is the premier works team in this season's competition. The finalists are Ryland' No. 1. and St. Helens Cable No. 1. and the games should be full of excilement. The Horse and Jockey green is in fine trim, and it is to be hoped that the weather will be all that is desired. After the gsmes, which will commence at three o'clock prompt, Mrs. W. Webster will present the cup and watches to the players. Rylands' players will wear red rosettes and the Cable team white rosettes, in order that the public can readily distinguish each team. RECODS OF THE FINALISTS. Below, we give a record of the teams during the competition : RYLANDS' TEAM : Round Team defeated Ist Houghton's 2nd White Lead Carpenters and Joiners Richmond's Na)lor's</p>
        <p>Majority</p>
        <p>3rd 4th Semi-final CABLE CO's. TEAM:</p>
        <p>Ist 2nd 3rd 4th Semi-final</p>
        <p>&amp; K. Fitters Fe,,nell-street Tannery Fletcher's Mouldere Howley Tannery County Asylum</p>
        <p>Fletober's Moulders were the winners last sear, and Howley Tannery were the runners-up. TO-DAY'S TEAMS. The following teams will do duty to-day : Rylands No. 4, St. Helens Cable No. L sor. Carrington ... 5 2 Allen ... 1 North ... 2 Clarke ... 1 Tweedie 2 Seymour (oapt.y 2 Bridbury '2 Unsworth 3 ItichirdLon 2 F‘llows 2 Timmins Harrison</p>
