      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-08-09_WidnesExaminer_art0226" n="art0226">
        <head>ANNUAL HANDICAP.</head>
        <p>ANNUAL HANDICAP.</p>
        <p>Draw for the Ist Round of Great Competition</p>
        <p>The gigantic annual handicap promoted by the Warrington Works Bowling Association will be opened on Saturday next. There is an exceedingly large entry, and the first prize, given by Lady Greenall, is valued at £5 55., the winner also holding the " Greens,' " Cop for one year. ci'aptain 0 R. Crosfield will give the second prize, value £3 Sc. he games will ben up, with a limit of seven, and will commence promptly to time. Anyone falling to respond to his name within 15 minutes will be struck out. Tbis rule will be strictly enforced. 'I he draw for the second round will be made at two o'clock each Saturday, so that winners of the first round may upon application to the secretary ascertain the exact time they will be required to play in the second round. No grace whatever will be allowed for this round, and competitors are requested to assist the committee by being punctual. The draw for the first round next Saturday is as follows : _</p>
      </div>
