      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-08-09_WidnesExaminer_art0245" n="art0245">
        <head>CHESTER.</head>
        <p>CHESTER.</p>
        <p>POOP The Dee at Chester gave us po results, on lug to the holidays. With the exception of a few dafpe, nothing was done, the bream berg entirely off feed. The canal WBt: better, a fair bag of roach being taken, while eels were so plentiful that tackle, was broken, time after time. A very nice bream was also taken from the canal near the town. The length of this canal in town seems to fish better than the more favoured spots, such as Tatenall- road or Beeston.</p>
      </div>
