        <p>TO BE SOLD Olt LET. A very attractive Country Residence in beautiful gardens and well-wooded grounds. " HALL NOOK," PENKETH, near WARRINGTON. The residence is a handsome red brick structure, containing a square hall with w.c. and lavatory off; Dining-room with oak panelled dado and handsome grate and overmantel; Drawing-room fitted with mahogany Inglenook and bookshelves with over- mantel to match; Morning room; Ten Bedrooms. 2 with lavatory (basins fitted); Bathroom, separate w.c.. large boxroom. observatory roof, conservatory, lounee and greenhouse entered from the house. Excellent kitchen, butler's pantry, scullery, larder on ground floor and very dry and cool cellars. One of the upstairs rooms is large enough for a billiard room. The outbuildings include a very prolific vinery. peachhouse. orchid house, zmlsh- room house, potting sheds, &amp;c., and in an enclosed yard are 2-stall stable and loosebox, coachhouse, harness room, motor garage, dog kennels, man's rooms. There is a large rose garden and a fruit. flower and kitchen garden and velvet lawn. The grounds are beautifully planted with ornamental trees, shrubs and plants of mature growth, with qumnterhouses in convenient positions. Town gas, water and drainage. The tenure is freehold. Area of land about 5 acres. More land could be addei, or an offer for the house and a portion of the' grounds might be entertained. For further particulars apply to Messrs. John White and Co.. Estate Office, Warrington; or to MEFSRS. BOTTLT. SON &amp; MAPLES. LAND AGENTS Ar, AUCTIONEERS, 3, COOK-STREET, LIVERPOOL.</p>
