        <p>H I PPOD ROME &amp; Palace, Warrington. 7-0 orvinociE NIGiTLY 9-0 MONDAY NEXT, AUGUST 11th, 1913• Special Matinee on THURSDAY, August 14th, and SATURDAY, August 16tit at 2-30. THE WORLD'S GREATEST CONJUROR e uNG LING see • In a performance of Oriental:splendour and weird mysticism. CHUNG LING SOO, assisted by Miss SURE SEEN and a large staff of Chinese Assistants, presents in rapid succession, the most beautiful, Baffling, and Interesting Series of Illusions ever submitted to the public. CHUNG LING SOO will offer his entertainment in two parts. Part 1. THE WILLOW PATTERN PLATE, In which Quaint and Exquisite Manipulative Tricks amuse and bewilder the most astute minds. Part 2. Chung Ling Soo will introduce ASLEEP IN THE AIR. The most Perplexing allu Bewilder,vg Experiment of its kind in the World. The LIVING TARGET. The Shooting of an Arrow with a Cord attached through the body of Miss SURE SEEN THE BIRTH OF THE PEARL. The Prettiest illusion ever presented. A large shell mounted on a rich carved pedestal. At a signal, the shell slowly opens, disclosing a large Pink Pearl, which changes ins mysterious manner to a beautiful maiden. THE MAGIC CAULDRON. The Cauldron is filled with water from buckets handed to Chung Ling Soo by attendants: a lire is lighted under the cauldron. As the pot is merrily boiling there appear 4 Irons the c.oud of steam—Doves, Rabbits, liens, etc., until the stage represents a Farmyard, when amidst the steam appears the human form of Miss Suee Seen. THE MYSTIC BOTTLE. In the first, the stage being quite clear, there will be placed upon it, six cases containing two dozen bottles of beer each, making in all 12 • dozen boales. These are shown to the audience. They are then set one upon the other on an elevated stand clear above the stage. An empty coverovhich is proven to be so, is then placed over these cases, immediately removed, disclosing the fact that the whole of the bottles have disappeared, and in the place of them stands a mammoth bottle, the label on it forms a door from which emerges a Chinese girl beautifully gowned. THE CREATION OF A BUTTERFLY. On a smell wooden frame a piece of blank paper is stretched. This is hung on a thin cord placed across the stage. A Silkworm is drawn upon the paper, which bursting, reveals a largo golden Cocoon. The frame is removed, the cocoon opens, and a Chinese girl emerges like an Oriental Butterfly. A DREAM OF WEALTH. A Ladies' Trinket Box is placed on a stand, which-in turn is placed upon a table. Milk is poured into the Casket, a spirit lamp lit underneath, and upon the Casket being, removed streams of, silver coins fall from it—then notes—then a .el,OOO note. This is suspended in mid-air, and instantly changes into an immense golden sovereign, which bursts into a star, frorn welch emerges a Chinese- lady, pouring forth golden sovereigns from a horn of plenty. Rich Taylor, the Whistling Ventriloquist, in a new. and novel Whistling, Singing, and Ventriloquial Scene. Expensive Engagement of GEORGE SHELDON Inv,n Careless, V. C. and F. RAWnoN BUCKLEY'S Company in Captain Hippodrome Perfection Pictures. I Rene Ralph Dainty Character Comeoienne. Mignon and Frasettis, In an Artistic Dancing and Musical Act. Gallery, 2.1., early doors,3d. Pit, 4d., curly doors, 6d. Grand Circle, 6d.. early doors, 90. Stall% le., early doors, 1/3, booked and reserved, lie. And in response to numerous CHUNG LING SOO MATINEES will be requests, two special given on THURSDAY, August 14th and SATURDAY, August 16th, at 2-30 p.m. On these occasions CHUNG LING SOO win present the whole of the afternoon's programme, and in addition to - his nightly performance, be will introduce Special Illusions. The Object of these Matinees is to afford an opportunity to those Ladies and Children who are not usual patrons of Vaudeville Entertainments to see CBUNG LING SOO'S Feast of Nagic, and the Management wish to draw special attention to the fact that NO OTHER ARTISTES will appear, and that Smoking will be Strictly Prohibited at these Matinees. Seats may now be booked at the Theatre. Tel. 500. Prices of Admission as Usual. Experience of other towns shows that Air ENTERTAINMENT MEE 'IIIIS IS GREATLY NEEDED, as every such Matinee given by CHUNG LING SOO has proved a phenomenal success.</p>
